{"title":"2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Whymath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Whymath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A sequence of squares is made of identical square tiles. The edge of each square is one tile length longer than the edge of the previous square. The first three squares are shown. How many more tiles does the seventh square require than the sixth?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/926b33e5dbe2d7e971f0ce8112e62c7a77b109a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] path p=origin--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle; draw(p); draw(shift(3,0)*p); draw(shift(3,1)*p); draw(shift(4,0)*p); draw(shift(4,1)*p); draw(shift(7,0)*p); draw(shift(7,1)*p); draw(shift(7,2)*p); draw(shift(8,0)*p); draw(shift(8,1)*p); draw(shift(8,2)*p); draw(shift(9,0)*p); draw(shift(9,1)*p); draw(shift(9,2)*p);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"78\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/e/9bedf76689c0129174a751e465fa79a69b763d24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 11 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 12 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 13 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 14 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5f0b29305e947b3755e0703980ff2aa077e72d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{\\text{th}}$\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" /> square has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and thus consists of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> tiles.\n</p><p>The seventh square thus has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/f/80fae7547c07a9074b05253e3569debdaddf5237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^2 = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" /> tiles while the sixth square has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242bade7eecb8dbe7d1ef62e8008cfb581dbe77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 = 36$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> tiles.  Therefore, the seventh square has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/7945d823589fe0516fc7613d7d5e2e125bb4a45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49-36=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"148\" height=\"30\" /> more tiles than the sixth square.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in solution 1, the sixth square has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the seventh square has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  A square of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> may be transformed into a square of side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> by adding a row of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tiles below, a column of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tiles to the right, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> tile directly below the new column and to the right of the new row, for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/b/f1bf06484d8286628f2a20d1be3c9a9b68d9667f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+6+1=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"161\" height=\"30\" /> added tiles.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in solution 1, the seventh square as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/026bb71c09708994ead7a4ee100a03960a87c4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> tiles while the sixth square has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8406a2a50c1aa1040c8862b912a5f3d703d9569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> tiles.  Thus the seventh square has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0f450a336636ba4b54a9ccd82b42bf52a2040b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^2 - 6^2 = (7+6)(7-6) = 13 \\cdot 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"343\" height=\"30\" /> more tiles than the sixth square.\n</p><p>~AkCANdo, edited by j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Whymath\">Video Solution by Whymath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Whymath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QGxNCcUB5zw\">https://youtu.be/QGxNCcUB5zw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8\" title=\"2002 AMC 8\">2002 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2002\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-ali